{"edits": [{"finding_ids": ["app/tickets.py:11:config-class"], "search": "from pydantic import BaseModel", "replace": "from pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict", "explanation": "ConfigDict is needed for the v2 model_config declaration that replaces the deprecated class-based Config. This is the import the finding's change requires."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/tickets.py:11:config-class"], "search": "    class Config:
        anystr_strip_whitespace = True", "replace": "    model_config = ConfigDict(str_strip_whitespace=True)", "explanation": "Pydantic v2 deprecates the class-based `class Config`. Per the v2 migration guide it is replaced by `model_config = ConfigDict(...)`, and the v1 option `anystr_strip_whitespace` is renamed to `str_strip_whitespace`. Behavior is unchanged: string fields are still stripped of surrounding whitespace."}], "notes": "Applied the config-class finding with two non-overlapping edits: add ConfigDict to the pydantic import, and replace the class Config block with model_config = ConfigDict(str_strip_whitespace=True).

Not changed, but needs a human decision: from_db_rows passes integer primary keys (per the comment) into `ticket_id: str`. Pydantic v1 coerced int to str, but Pydantic v2 does not coerce numbers to str by default, so this will raise a ValidationError at runtime. This is outside the listed finding, so I did not edit it. Options: convert in the caller (`ticket_id=str(r[0])`), or add `coerce_numbers_to_str=True` to the ConfigDict to keep v1 behavior. I recommend one of these as a follow-up. Also, the migration documentation section was empty, so the rename and the model_config pattern come from the standard v2 migration guide rather than retrieved docs."}
